# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored, never commit real secrets) for
# local `wrangler dev` runs. Real values are set in production via
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` — see ../README.md.

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather. Leave unset locally to run telegram.ts
# in "dry-run" mode (logs outbound sends to the console, returns a fake
# message id) so the rest of the flow is testable without a real bot.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Your numeric Telegram chat id (see README for how to find it). Required
# for the webhook handler to verify inbound replies actually come from you.
# TELEGRAM_OWNER_CHAT_ID=

# A random string you make up yourself. Set the same value on the Telegram
# side via `setWebhook`'s `secret_token` param — see README. Used to verify
# inbound webhook calls are really from Telegram and not a random POST.
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
